    "url": "https://facebook.com/hisham.b.hashim.75/posts/a-light-that-never-dimmed-remembering-dr-abdul-latif-alwisome-messages-arrive-li/10238411201073496",
    "title": "Hisham Badrul Hashim Spice",
    "description": "“Salam, Latiff has passed away this morning, 10.00 am @ PPUM…” It was a simple message from Kak Rauzah Hashim, carrying only a handful of words. Yet within those few syllables lived the weight of an entire lifetime. Soon followed the familiar funeral announcement from Masjid Al-Madaniah, the solemn Arabic prayers, the times for the final journey, and the gentle reminder that every schedule in this world ultimately answers only to Allah’s decree.\n\nwith something useful, something meaningful, and something that helps them see the world more clearly. That, in many ways, was Abang Latif’s gift to everyone. Born on Merdeka Day in Johor Bahru, educated at Sekolah Dato’ Jaafar where he proudly served as Drum Major, he spent his life leading—not by standing in front of crowds, but by quietly walking beside people. As a lecturer at the University of Malaya specialising in Traffic Management Systems, he understood roads professionally, yet somehow understood life’s journeys even better.\n\nSome people measure friendship by the number of messages they send. Others measure it by showing up when showing up hurts. That afternoon, despite his own illness, his quiet presence spoke more eloquently than any speech ever could. It reminded us that loyalty does not disappear when strength fades. Sometimes it shines brightest precisely because strength has faded. This evening, I walked into Masjid Al-Madaniah to bid him farewell before joining the congregational funeral prayer.\n\nFarewell, dear Abang Latif. Thank you for showing us that wisdom need not be loud, kindness never grows old, and friendship requires neither constant meetings nor elaborate promises—only a faithful heart. May Allah forgive every shortcoming, accept every good deed, widen your resting place, illuminate your grave with His mercy, and grant you the everlasting company of the righteous.",
